suggest technical competence. Leadership good for crew cooperation. But show-off may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. Strengths: reliability (conscientious), stress resilience, weather assessment (technical), computer skills. Concerns: memory for numbers (attention/accuracy), nasty remarks (crew cooperation, professional communication). So mixed.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, but difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence. Concerns: communication, egocentric (crew cooperation), lack of development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: know-it-all (crew cooperation), hot temper (stress resilience, communication). So mixed.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Which candidate balances strengths and minimal concerns? Candidate B has strong reliability and stress handling but has nasty remarks and weak number memory. Number memory could be important for flight calculations. Nasty remarks severe for crew cooperation. Candidate C has good decision and calm but communication issues and egocentric. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but hot temper and know-it-all. Candidate A has leadership but show-off and not open to new ideas.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate B's reliability and stress handling are crucial, but nasty remarks could be disqualifying. Candidate C's calm and decision making are strong, but communication issues may be problematic. Candidate D's responsibility and problem solving are strong, but hot temper is concerning for stress resilience. Candidate A's anticipation and leadership are strong, but show-off and closed to ideas may affect crew.\n\nWe need to pick one. Perhaps Candidate C's ability to make correct decisions quickly, keep calm in crisis, understand complicated technology are core pilot criteria. Communication difficulty and egocentric are concerns but maybe can be mitigated with training. However, the panel should not ignore serious concerns. Egocentric and communication difficulty could affect crew cooperation heavily.\n\nCandidate B's nasty remarks are also serious. Might be disqualifying.\n\nCandidate D's hot temper is also serious.\n\nCandidate A's show-off and not open to new ideas also concerning.\n\nAll have concerns. Which has least severe? Maybe Candidate A's show-off is less severe than nasty remarks or hot temper? Not open to new ideas could affect adaptability. Show-off may affect crew but maybe manageable.\n\nCandidate A also has strong anticipation and leadership, which are valuable for long-distance flights.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate A as current provisional recommendation, noting concerns.\n\nWe need to reference discussion (none) but can say \"Given the facts we have so far\". Provide evidence: anticipation, complex connections, leadership, but also show-off and not open to new ideas.\n\nOk.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate A\"."}
