 need to follow the meeting process. The previous turn was Agent 1's public message (the one we just saw). Actually the system shows \"Round 1, Agent 1: Model thoughts before public response: ...\" and then a public response. So Agent 1 already gave a recommendation for Candidate B. Now it's our turn (Agent 3). We need to respond to the discussion, referencing Agent 1 and Agent 2. We need to state our current recommendation, possibly adjust based on evidence. We have our own notes (same as others). We need to consider the shared mental model: currently leading candidate is B (Agent 1), strong alternative A (Agent 2). We need to discuss other candidates C and D, and also address any missing criteria. We should bring up new aspects, perhaps ask for more info via tool calls if needed. But we can also give our own recommendation now, maybe still B, or maybe shift. Let's evaluate.\n\nWe have candidate facts:\n\nA: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, unfriendly, eats unhealthily, not open to new ideas.\n\nB: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills, regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks.\n\nC: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to consider criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility, etc.\n\nWe need to cover all candidates before final recommendation. So we should bring up candidate C or D now, perhaps compare them to B. We could ask a tool